v class=\"bullet-item\"><span class=\"marker\">&bull;</span>Dose related kidney damage</div>\n      <div class=\"bullet-item\"><span class=\"marker\">&bull;</span>Neutropenia, metabolic acidosis, uveitis and ocular hypotony also occur</div>\n\n      <div class=\"gap-small\"></div>\n\n      <div class=\"bullet-item\"><span class=\"marker red-marker\">&bull;</span><span class=\"note-label\">Note:</span> Probenecid must be coadministered with cidofovir to reduce the risk of nephrotoxicity, but probenecid itself causes rash, headache, fever, and nausea</div>\n\n      <div class=\"gap-small\"></div>\n\n      <div class=\"head-item\"><span class=\"marker\">&#10070;</span>Contraindications:</div>\n      <div class=\"bullet-item\"><span class=\"marker\">&bull;</span>Patients with preexisting renal impairment</div>\n      <div class=\"bullet-item\"><span class=\"marker\">&bull;</span>Patients taking concurrent nephrotoxic drugs, including NSAIDS</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>"
